  "map_info": {
    "description": "A manipulable quad-based object where you can drag cube corners. This map transitions from rigid relational closure to over-stabilization and manipulation. Quads relax the rigidity of triangles and introduce interactive constraint: agency within system limits. Geometry becomes something that can be touched and perturbed without collapsing.",
    "description_2": "Volume introduces enclosure and scalar comparison. With the emergence of bounded three-dimensional form, space becomes something that can be contained, filled, and compared. Through interaction with volumetric primitives, the player encounters scale not as abstraction but as bodily negotiation - how size, reach, and proximity reconfigure perception. The map establishes volume as the condition for material intuition in computational space.",
